## Rate Limiting

### Default Limits

| Plan | Requests/minute | Requests/day | Burst limit |
|------|----------------|--------------|-------------|
| Free | 10 | 1,000 | 20 |
| Basic | 60 | 10,000 | 100 |
| Pro | 300 | 100,000 | 500 |
| Enterprise | Unlimited | Unlimited | 1,000 |

### Rate Limit Headers

```http
X-RateLimit-Limit: 60
X-RateLimit-Remaining: 59
X-RateLimit-Reset: 1640995200
X-RateLimit-Retry-After: 60
```

### Handling Rate Limits

```typescript
const response = await fetch('/api/ai/chat', {
  method: 'POST',
  headers: {
    'Content-Type': 'application/json',
    'Authorization': `Bearer ${apiKey}`
  },
  body: JSON.stringify({ message: 'Hello' })
});

if (response.status === 429) {
  const retryAfter = response.headers.get('X-RateLimit-Retry-After');
  console.log(`Rate limited. Retry after ${retryAfter} seconds`);

  // Wait and retry
  await new Promise(resolve => setTimeout(resolve, retryAfter * 1000));
  // Retry request...
}
```

## Error Handling

### Standard Error Format

```typescript
{
  "success": false,
  "error": {
    "code": "INVALID_REQUEST",
    "message": "The request is missing required parameters",
    "details": {
      "missing_fields": ["message"]
    },
    "request_id": "req_123"
  }
}
```

### Error Codes

| Code | HTTP Status | Description |
|------|-------------|-------------|
| `INVALID_REQUEST` | 400 | Missing or invalid parameters |
| `UNAUTHORIZED` | 401 | Invalid API key or session |
| `FORBIDDEN` | 403 | Insufficient permissions |
| `NOT_FOUND` | 404 | Resource not found |
| `RATE_LIMITED` | 429 | Rate limit exceeded |
| `INTERNAL_ERROR` | 500 | Server error |
| `SERVICE_UNAVAILABLE` | 503 | HF Spaces backend unavailable |

### Error Handling Best Practices

```typescript
try {
  const response = await fetch('/api/ai/chat', {
    method: 'POST',
    headers: {
      'Content-Type': 'application/json',
      'Authorization': `Bearer ${apiKey}`
    },
    body: JSON.stringify({ message: 'Hello' })
  });

  if (!response.ok) {
    const error = await response.json();

    switch (error.error.code) {
      case 'RATE_LIMITED':
        // Handle rate limiting
        const retryAfter = response.headers.get('X-RateLimit-Retry-After');
        await wait(retryAfter * 1000);
        return retryRequest();

      case 'UNAUTHORIZED':
        // Refresh auth token
        await refreshAuth();
        return retryRequest();

      case 'SERVICE_UNAVAILABLE':
        // Fallback to cached response or show maintenance message
        return getCachedResponse() || showMaintenanceMessage();

      default:
        throw new Error(error.error.message);
    }
  }

  return await response.json();
} catch (error) {
  console.error('API request failed:', error);
  throw error;
}
```

